# Copy to .env.local for development; set the same names in Vercel for production.
# Without any channel, forms log to the console in development and return
# 503 in production (the site then tells the visitor to use WhatsApp).

# --- Google Sheet (preferred) ---------------------------------------------
# 1. Google Cloud console: create a project, enable the "Google Sheets API",
#    create a Service Account, add a JSON key and download it.
# 2. Create an empty Google Sheet. Share it with the service account's
#    client_email as Editor. Copy the ID from the URL:
#    https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS_PART>/edit
# 3. Paste the whole key file as one line below (or base64-encode it).
# Tabs "Volunteer sign-up", "Internship application" and "Website message"
# are created on first submission, with headers.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID=
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# --- Generic webhook (fallback) --------------------------------------------
# Used only when the Google Sheet variables are not set. Receives a JSON POST
# { form, title, submittedAt, values, text } (Slack, Discord, Make, Zapier).
FORM_WEBHOOK_URL=
